{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And we passed by our brothers, the children of Esau, who dwell in Seir, by way of the Arabah, from Elath and from Ezion-geber.</b> We passed by the darkened paths (דרכים הערבים) that are in the Torah, and by the does (איילותיה) of the Torah, and 'from Ezion-geber' (מעציון גבר) — just as Ezion-geber is for the man (גברא) of the world, of whom they say 'We will do and we will hear' (נעשה ונשמע) yet do not do so. Thus they said in the Midrash Rabbah."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "The comment is built on Aramaic wordplay: ערבה/ערבים (dark/bitter), אילת/איילות (does — a rabbinic epithet for Torah), and עציון גבר read as 'the counsel (עצה) of the man (גברא).' Rendered hyper-literally; the final clause 'of whom they say… yet do not do so' is textually difficult and left as found."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:44:51.161139863Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}